  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39499466",
      "title": "Changing Data with Mutations",
      "sourceHash": "838d4c407ccc384e3e73552a8c58420c1ca880c0193a21380a1d364de3dfb208",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.06,
          "en": "Okay, so at this point we did a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.06,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "of data fetching and we learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 9.18,
          "en": "about the internals and the behavior of React Query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.18,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "But React Query cannot just be used to get data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 17.81,
          "en": "but also to send data, to create a new event, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 21.03,
          "en": "Now for that we can click this button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.03,
          "end": 26.03,
          "en": "to open this component, this new event component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "which opens in such a modal and we can now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "that we collect that data entered by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 37.743,
          "en": "and then use React Query to send it to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "Because this backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "which I'm providing to you also has a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 48.27,
          "en": "for accepting post requests to slash events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 53.27,
          "en": "to store a new event in that dummy events JSON file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 54.813,
          "en": "which we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.67,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "So therefore, in this new event component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "the question now is how can we use useQuery",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 65.553,
          "en": "to send that data and how can we collect that data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.14,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "Now collecting will actually be easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 70.869,
          "en": "because in there we got this event form component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.869,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "which I prepared for you, where I simply output that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 78.813,
          "en": "and where I then get all that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 84,
          "en": "So in this new event JSX file, we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "that this data is also sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 90.56,
          "en": "And for this, we should again import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.56,
          "end": 95.56,
          "en": "from React Query as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "And that something now is a different hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "It's not useQuery anymore because you only use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 105.003,
          "en": "useQuery to get data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "To send data, to send a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 110.58,
          "en": "as we plan to do it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 114.42,
          "en": "you would instead use use mutation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now just to be clear, you could also send post requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "with use Query because after all, you're writing the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 126.063,
          "en": "for sending the requests on your own anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "But this use mutation hook is optimized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 134.403,
          "en": "for such data changing queries, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.403,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "simply by making sure that those requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "are not sent instantly when this component renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "as it by default is the case with use Query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 149.13,
          "en": "But that instead requests are only sent when you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 151.293,
          "en": "to send them, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.147,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "from inside this handle submit function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 158.67000000000002,
          "en": "So use mutation it is, and we should therefore call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 161.736,
          "en": "in this new event component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.736,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "And just like useQuery, use mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 167.253,
          "en": "takes a configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.122,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now here we must set a mutation function now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "just as we had to set a Query function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 179.99,
          "en": "for the useQuery, we can also set a mutation key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 180.99,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "But you don't necessarily need to do this because the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 190.44,
          "en": "with mutations typically isn't to cache their response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.44,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "because they are primarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "about changing something on your backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 198.813,
          "en": "not about getting and storing data in your fronted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 200.13,
          "end": 204.45,
          "en": "So therefore here I'll just set up the mutation function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 204.45,
          "end": 206.8,
          "en": "and I'll add a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 207.663,
          "end": 209.94,
          "en": "to this HTDP JS file for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 212.25,
          "en": "Now to save you some time and make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 212.25,
          "end": 215.13,
          "en": "that you don't have to write all that code on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 215.13,
          "end": 216.69,
          "en": "attached to this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 221.37,
          "en": "you find an updated HTDP.JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "which contains this create new event function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 228.19299999999998,
          "en": "that's being exported, which will in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.19299999999998,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "send this post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 233.013,
          "en": "to the backend that will create that event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "This function wants the event data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.13,
          "en": "as an input and it's now function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.13,
          "end": 242.223,
          "en": "which we can use in the new event JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 248.33,
          "en": "So here we should import, create new event from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 251.19,
          "end": 255.22,
          "en": "and then going up and going up util H to the P JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 256.77,
          "end": 260.087,
          "en": "and then set create new event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.087,
          "end": 263.943,
          "en": "as a value for this mutation function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 266.91,
          "en": "Just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 266.91,
          "end": 269.76,
          "en": "And even though this create new event function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 269.76,
          "end": 271.44,
          "en": "needs some input data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "we don't have to wrap it with an anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "because I'll show you how you can pass data to that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 279.273,
          "en": "in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.31,
          "end": 284.13,
          "en": "Because just as before with useQuery,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 284.13,
          "end": 287.073,
          "en": "useMutation will return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 287.073,
          "end": 289.77,
          "en": "and we can destructure this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 289.77,
          "end": 292.98,
          "en": "to get access to some useful properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 292.98,
          "end": 294.591,
          "en": "Now as you see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 294.591,
          "end": 297.81,
          "en": "we again got quite some properties to access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.81,
          "end": 301.92,
          "en": "for example, also a data property so that we could work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.92,
          "end": 304.68,
          "en": "with the data that might be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 304.68,
          "end": 307.54,
          "en": "in the response of that request we're sending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 310.95,
          "en": "but I don't need that data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.95,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "Instead, this object also has a mutate property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 316.62,
          "en": "which is extremely important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 316.62,
          "end": 319.8,
          "en": "because this is now a function which you can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.8,
          "end": 323.89,
          "en": "anywhere in this component to actually send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 324.81,
          "end": 326.372,
          "en": "because as mentioned, useMutation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 326.372,
          "end": 331.137,
          "en": "unlike useQuery does not automatically send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 331.137,
          "end": 333.403,
          "en": "when this component here is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 333.403,
          "end": 337.92,
          "en": "but instead only when you tell it to send that request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 337.92,
          "end": 341.15999999999997,
          "en": "which you do with help of that mutate function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 341.15999999999997,
          "end": 343.29,
          "en": "And it's of course here in handle submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 343.29,
          "end": 345.9,
          "en": "where I wanna send that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 345.9,
          "end": 349.8,
          "en": "Here I can call mutate and then in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 349.8,
          "end": 352.653,
          "en": "pass my form data to mutate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.7,
          "end": 356.67,
          "en": "Now I actually have to change the form data a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 356.67,
          "end": 358.98,
          "en": "to have the right format for the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 358.98,
          "end": 362.76,
          "en": "here in this demo app I'll wrap it in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 362.76,
          "end": 364.92,
          "en": "where I have an event property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 364.92,
          "end": 367.683,
          "en": "which holds my form data as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 368.88,
          "end": 370.56,
          "en": "And of course, the exact shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.56,
          "end": 372.54,
          "en": "of data you want to send here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 372.54,
          "end": 374.01,
          "en": "depends on the shape of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 374.01,
          "end": 376.02,
          "en": "you are getting in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 376.02,
          "end": 379.17,
          "en": "and the shape of data your backend wants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 379.17,
          "end": 380.64,
          "en": "Here this will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 380.64,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "that I'm sending the data exactly as required to my backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 388.59,
          "en": "And that's again, all you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 388.59,
          "end": 393.59000000000003,
          "en": "This will send this request whenever this form is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 393.72,
          "end": 397.053,
          "en": "and it will do so with help of React Query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 398.58,
          "end": 403.58,
          "en": "So if I now save this and I go back and I enter test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 409.01,
          "en": "and this is a test and I pick some date and some time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 409.38,
          "end": 414.38,
          "en": "and some location, if I click create, nothing happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 420.48,
          "end": 422.61,
          "en": "well it makes sense that nothing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 422.61,
          "end": 425.85,
          "en": "because we haven't written any code that would do anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 425.85,
          "end": 428.34,
          "en": "after sending that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 428.34,
          "end": 431.55,
          "en": "We're not navigating away or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 431.55,
          "end": 433.432,
          "en": "even though we'll soon do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 433.432,
          "end": 438.432,
          "en": "But in addition, if we open the developer tools, we can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 439.41,
          "end": 442.86,
          "en": "that we got an error, that I got back an error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 442.86,
          "end": 444.093,
          "en": "as it turns out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 445.29,
          "end": 448.38,
          "en": "And if I open the network tab and I try sending this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 448.38,
          "end": 452.013,
          "en": "I again get an error here, a bad request error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 453.78,
          "end": 458.78,
          "en": "And in my preview tab here where I see the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 458.82,
          "end": 463.82,
          "en": "I got back, I see this message invalid data provided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 465,
          "end": 468.51,
          "en": "And if I take a look at my backend code, I can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 468.51,
          "end": 472.56,
          "en": "that this is text I'm sending back as a 400.",
          "zh": ""
